 224: ## Course-level checks
 225: 
 226: | Check | After unit | Check days | Respond days | What it checks |
 227: |---|---|---|---|---|
 228: | Course-level check, mid-year (week 13; it is unit 2's end-of-unit assessment) | 2 | 1 | 1 | Day 13 scores unit 2 in full with unseen items and samples unit 1. Unit 2: on paper, order the step-cards of each part of a new pictured job (E1-ALG-PS-01); circle which pictured machine chose by finding a pattern in examples, and draw a new card into the group a pattern-finder would guess (E1-ALG-ML-02); sort new activity cards into people do well, computers do well and both (E1-SOC-HU-15). Spoken, in five groups of six: from two new orders of the same steps, say why the results differ (E1-ALG-IM-03), and give the reason for one activity card's place (E1-SOC-HU-15), recorded as two separate look-fors. Unit 1 sampled: a new share-or-private card with what to do if asked (E1-SYS-SE-12) and a new rule scene judged with its consequence (E1-SYS-IM-13); unit 1's end-of-unit record for E1-SYS-HW-11 is carried unscored. Whole-class paper task of about 15 minutes. Day 14, the respond day for unit 2 and the check, reteaches by error letter and gathers fresh evidence on the missed items |
 229: | Course-level check, year-end (week 27; it is unit 4's end-of-unit assessment) | 4 | 1 | 1 | Day 27 scores unit 4 in full with unseen items and samples units 1 to 3. Unit 4: in the spoken groups, each child collects one count (counting or measuring a new object in cubes) and one description (looking at it) and records both on a record card (E1-DAT-DC-08); on paper, sort new question cards, read aloud, into "count or look to find out" and "a feeling, guess or idea" (E1-DAT-DI-09); spoken, from a new picture of a school need, say who the question helps, and from a new wording pair, say what the changed word changes (E1-DAT-IM-10). Units 1 to 3 sampled with three short new items: what a new event program does when tapped (E1-PRO-RD-06), the first wrong block in a new program, circled and fixed by drawing the moved block (E1-PRO-TR-07), and a new pretend login card (E1-SYS-SE-12); unit 3's end-of-unit record, including the program each child laid out (E1-PRO-PD-04) and the changing-value sort (E1-PRO-VD-05), is carried unscored. Unit 5 follows in weeks 29 to 32 and is checked by its own end-of-unit assessment. Day 28, the respond day for unit 4 and the check, reteaches and records each child's support and gains for grade 2 |
