boundary asks neither), no copyright, misinformation or digital footprint. End-of-unit (day 5): a new part-and-job card match with one part named and its purpose said aloud (E1-SYS-HW-11); a new rule scene, saying why the rule matters and what happens to self and class if it is broken (E1-SYS-IM-13); a new pretend login card, circling what stays secret and the sign-out button, and saying what to do if asked for it (E1-SYS-SE-12); respond day 6. Tools: device stations (any school device, its home screen only, job: matching parts to jobs; the teacher's sign-out shown on one screen). Curio Class writes: the part-and-job picture cards with adapted parts, the rule story cards, the paper pretend login and the share-or-private sort set | First because the rules and the parts' names must exist before the year's first device turn (session 3) and every device day of unit 3; responsible use opens the unit so the device turn happens under rules the class has just explained. Keep-safe sits with the rules as a rule for keeping our information safe, taught on paper. Base: archived Year 2 "IT around us" lessons 1 and 5 | Candidate: kept, a station rotation plan for a room with three devices on session 3, zero added days | Some children use adapted devices or tools: talk is about what a part lets a person do, never about a classmate; use the wording the sensitivity read settles from its pack. Some homes have no device and some have many: no child is asked what is at home. Passwords: no real password, name or address is said or written; the teacher page carries health's "If a student tells you something" steps word for word. Devices carried with two hands, cords behind the table, no food or drink near them, headphone volume set by the teacher. Agent reads: sensitivity (the starting pack in Sensitivity reads first). |
