Measuring in cubes (unit 4 sessions 1 and 2, weeks 23 and 24) uses no lean row, but math grade 1 teaches length
units in its unit 6 (days 111 to 128, weeks 23 to 26), the same weeks. If math is later, the unit measures by laying
linking cubes end to end along the plant and counting them together with the teacher, with no gaps or overlaps shown
on the record card, which needs only the counting of math unit 1; comparing taller and shorter directly is
kindergarten math. No row leans on English language arts, science or social studies. Speaking and listening
(explaining a program, following a partner's cards, saying why a question fits) are practiced here, not owned; the
